(version 1)

# Same-footprint-instance hole clearance: on the IM72D128 (LLGA-5-4) mic
# footprint, the bottom-port acoustic vent (NPTH, 0.8mm drill) sits only
# 0.205mm from the adjacent mechanical/ground pad "5" -- real vendor package
# geometry (IFX-PG-LLGA-5-4's own footprint/3D model), not a placement error.
# Every one of the 96 mic instances trips the board's general 0.25mm
# hole-clearance rule identically for this reason. "A.Reference == B.Reference"
# scopes this to pad/hole pairs belonging to the same physical component
# instance -- an intra-footprint clearance is a fixed fact of the part's own
# geometry, never something board layout can fix, so it's safe to loosen here
# without touching the 0.25mm rule anywhere else on the board (hole-to-hole,
# hole-to-copper between DIFFERENT components is untouched).
(rule "intra-footprint hole clearance (real package geometry)"
	(condition "A.Reference == B.Reference")
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 0.15mm))
)
